d States Erin  Sandusky owns g3 holistic in  California's Inland Empire the  Department of Justice gave him 14 days  to get out I turn white ja the floor it  was unexpected we all want the same  things I we don't want to seek more  crime we want to see less crime that's  why we have these places Sandusky got  into the medical marijuana industry two  years ago after leaving another line of  business behind I was in the mortgage  business for 20 years we were too small  to bail instead of too large to fail to  search out access patients have to go to  some places many of us would never  travel to and I thought that there was a  lot of work there that needed to be done  Sandusky's business sense proved right  and he soonduk spanned adjey's three  into several cities and even opened his  own grow house so that he could control  the quality of his product one of the  big problems and challenges that we've  been facing is one of the allegations of  profiteering a lot of times they don't  get to see what the back side is the  investments that we make not only  cultivation  research and that's not cheap obviously  there's no book that we can follow so a  lot of these things we have to come up  with ourselves that not only is  expensive but it takes a lot effort on a  lot of people's party dispensaries on  their face are any illegal operation  there's no Avenue in the law whatsoever  to accommodate the sales of marijuana  mark Brewster and Glenn Walsh members of  the California narcotic Officers  Association have a big problem with what  Sandusky is doing what the  administration has come out and said is  that they will support a states right to  have medical marijuana however if anyone  in that state is violating that law then  they will judiciously prosecute them I  think that's a very wide stance for them  to take and I look forward to them  exercising their jurisdiction in  California on November first 2011  officer Walsh got his wish the feds  raided all three of g3 stores as well as  the grow house this is the grow room  that I showed you last week this is one  of the grow rooms that we were in after  years of work and hundreds of thousands  of dollars spent this is what was left  of Sandusky's business  but they came in and uh and full raid  guns drawn Wow patients were handcuffed  some of our senior patients were  handcuffed and taken they seized all of  our assets my all of my personal assets  I got sixty dollars in my pocket that's  it I don't I don't have nothing what's  the future hold for you and for g3 I  don't even know officials from the  Department of Justice would not  participate in an on camera interview  but according to the search warrant the  DEA rated Sandusky's three stores as  well as his home and the home of his  colleague because marijuana has a  schedule one controlled substance which  under federal law means that it is not  recognized as having any medical value  and any possession distribution or  cultivation is a violation of federal  law marijuana is not modern medicine and  people will try to say well there need  to be more studies there there has to be  more studies when we look at marijuana  marijuana has been studied and studied  and studied but the American Medical  Association said just the opposite in  2009 urging that marijuana's status is a  federal schedule one controlled  substance be reviewed with the goal of  facilitating the conduct of clinical  research and development of cannabinoid  based medicines if I take the big pharma  medications that they had me on in 2001  I would not have a liver and then I die  I don't get high anymore it just takes  my pain away I was diagnosed with HIV 15  years ago the same year that prop 215  was passed it is helping me to increase  my appetite it gives me the energy to  come here in protest for people that I  know that are sicker than me another  portion of the search warrant reads the  sale for profit of marijuana including  sales inside of marijuana stores may  constitute a violation of California's  medical marijuana laws when we  collectively or cooperatively get  together to cultivate marijuana we can  do that and if it's my land and I would  like to help you cultivate your  marijuana I can do that you cannot  however reimburse me for any expenses we  don't all grow our own lettuce tomatoes  pickles you know we go to the store we  pick those up so and that many of those  patients are too sick to even try so  you've got to be able to trust somebody  to do it for you and that's where we get  the necessity for a club because you  know we put those professionals in place  that know how to do it I don't believe  that that portion of the law involving  reimbursement or financial gain from the  growing of marijuana I don't think  that's a problem at all i think it's a  very good sound basis when you have that  much of the substance that much cash  then you also have the other problems  that come with it and the violence  that's behind that much money in that  business is incredible as you can see  from some of the border violence we have  going on but Sandusky is in fueling the  cartels by importing their product he  grows his own reports his profits pays  his taxes his reward for this diligence  they'll lose energy  so what's the little one behind Wow as  well I mean I'm what are they gonna do  to me thrown in jail yes and yet as the  feds step up enforcement against medical  marijuana a growing portion of the  population is beginning to lean towards  all out legalization I was original one  of the original drug wires when Nixon  announced the war on drugs I let the  narcotic enforcement ever occur the city  of Los Angeles in those years and since  that time I have come to see the damage  that prohibition has done to our country  and our communities and especially our  young people make it legal in charge  taxes on it instead of putting the money  in the pockets of the real criminals the  Mexican cartels don't get me